    "raw_asr": "uh basically diagnose and reconfigure the stm thirty two c a n bus peripheral after observing continuous error passive flags and transmission aborts across the automotive network follow these diagnostic steps to restore communication stability first halt all active transmission mailboxes buy setting the a b r q bit in register c a n dash t s r to discard failed transmission frames cleanly second recalculate bit timing parameters four five hundred kilobits per second operation buy configuring prescaler twelve time segment one to eleven and time segment two to four in c a n dash b t r third configure receive filter bank zero in mask mode to accept only standard identifiers zero x one zero zero through zero x one zero f into f i f o zero fourth clear the bus off condition buy cycling the i n r q bit in c a n dash m c r to re enter normal operational mode safely across all active network nodes and bus transceivers connected to the physical cable harness",
    "refined_text": "Diagnose and reconfigure the STM32 CAN bus peripheral after observing continuous error-passive flags and transmission aborts across the automotive network. Follow these diagnostic steps to restore communication stability:\n\n1. Halt all active transmission mailboxes by setting the `ABRQ` bit in register `CAN_TSR` to discard failed transmission frames cleanly.\n2. Recalculate bit timing parameters for 500kbps operation by configuring prescaler 12, time segment 1 to 11, and time segment 2 to 4 in `CAN_BTR`.\n3. Configure receive filter bank 0 in mask mode to accept only standard identifiers `0x100` through `0x10F` into FIFO 0.\n4. Clear the bus-off condition by cycling the `INRQ` bit in `CAN_MCR` to re-enter normal operational mode safely across all active network nodes and physical CAN bus transceivers connected to the harness."
