    "refined_text": "Configure continuous high-speed analog data acquisition on the RP2040 microcontroller using dual DMA ping-pong channels to capture sensor waveforms at 500ksps. Execute these hardware configuration steps across RP2040 registers in sequential order:\n\n1. Initialize ADC channel 0 on dedicated analog GPIO pin 26 and enable the internal clock divider for continuous free-running sampling mode.\n2. Configure primary DMA channel 0 to transfer conversion results from register `ADC_FIFO` to memory buffer A.\n3. Configure secondary DMA channel 1 to chain from channel 0 and fill memory buffer B when buffer A transfer completes successfully.\n4. Enable DMA interrupts on buffer completion to process incoming analog blocks asynchronously without dropping conversion data or overflowing ring buffers in memory across active sample windows to sustain uninterrupted continuous streaming data collection."
