    "refined_text": "Configure the U-Boot bootloader on an embedded ARM target board to download and execute a development Linux kernel image over the local network via TFTP. Follow these operational setup steps in the serial bootloader console environment:\n\n1. Assign static network parameters in the U-Boot prompt by setting `ipaddr` to 192.168.1.100 and `serverip` to 192.168.1.10 on the local development network subnet.\n2. Load the compiled production kernel image into DRAM memory by running `tftp 0x80000000 uImage` across the physical Ethernet interface.\n3. Load the compiled Devicetree binary into RAM using `tftp 0x88000000 board.dtb` to provide hardware descriptors.\n4. Boot the Linux kernel with `bootm 0x80000000 - 0x88000000` to start operating system initialization and verify kernel console output messages without encountering kernel panic errors or mounting root filesystem failures."
