    "refined_text": "Diagnose an unexpected STM32 HardFault exception caused by a null pointer dereference inside an interrupt handler using OpenOCD and GDB. Follow these diagnostic debugging procedures to systematically analyze the processor fault stack frame:\n\n1. Attach GDB to the running OpenOCD target by executing `arm-none-eabi-gdb` followed by `target remote localhost:3333`.\n2. Read the memory address stored in the Process Stack Pointer register by issuing `info registers psp` in the GDB console.\n3. Inspect the exception stack frame at the PSP address to extract the stacked Program Counter (`PC`) register value.\n4. Use the `list` command at the extracted program counter address to pinpoint the exact line of C code responsible for triggering the memory fault during execution, and inspect local register variables to understand the precise failure condition."
