    "refined_text": "Implement a low-latency interrupt deferral pattern in FreeRTOS to offload serial packet processing from the UART ISR to a worker thread. Follow these firmware implementation steps to minimize interrupt latency and avoid priority inversion:\n\n1. Create the high-priority serial worker task and initialize its task handle pointer for notification targeting.\n2. In the UART receive ISR, read the hardware data register `UART_DR` and push the incoming received byte into a dedicated thread-safe lock-free ring buffer in memory.\n3. Send an asynchronous task notification from the ISR by calling `vTaskNotifyGiveFromISR()`.\n4. In the worker task, wait for notification by calling `ulTaskNotifyTake()` and process queued bytes without keeping interrupts disabled unnecessarily across long frame handling routines in firmware execution while guaranteeing high-throughput reliable packet processing under high load."
