    "refined_text": "Implement robust multi-thread liveliness supervision on an automotive STM32 controller using the hardware Window Watchdog (`WWDG`). Follow these functional safety procedures to protect against intermittent firmware execution hangs:\n\n1. Configure the window watchdog prescaler division factor and window upper threshold in register `WWDG_CFR` to define an allowable refresh window between 20ms and 60ms.\n2. Create a dedicated watchdog manager task running at a deterministic fixed 50ms periodic tick rate in FreeRTOS.\n3. Collect liveliness heartbeat bitmasks from all safety-critical application tasks before attempting to service the hardware timer.\n4. Write the refreshed counter value to register `WWDG_CR` only if all tasks have reported valid heartbeats within the legal timing window without exception across operational cycles in safety-critical environments, ensuring fail-safe system reset behavior whenever deadlines are missed."
