    "refined_text": "Implement an automated bus recovery routine for an STM32 I2C peripheral when a slave sensor holds the serial data line low following an unexpected master reset. Follow these automated bus recovery steps to safely release the locked two-wire bus:\n\n1. Disable the I2C peripheral by clearing the `PE` bit in control register `I2C_CR1`.\n2. Reconfigure the SCL and SDA pins as open-drain general-purpose outputs using `GPIO_MODER`.\n3. Generate nine clock pulses on the SCL line by toggling the GPIO pin until the stuck slave device releases the SDA line completely.\n4. Generate a hardware stop condition by asserting SDA high while SCL is high, and reinitialize the I2C master peripheral safely to resume communication without requiring hardware power cycling or interrupting adjacent devices on the shared bus."
