    "refined_text": "Partition an onboard eMMC storage device and install the U-Boot second-stage bootloader on an embedded Linux Cortex-A system. Follow these embedded system installation procedures to prepare boot partitions, configure block storage parameters, and format persistent storage:\n\n1. Write the primary bootloader `MLO` binary to the eMMC boot0 hardware partition using `dd if=MLO of=/dev/mmcblk0boot0 bs=1k`.\n2. Flash the U-Boot image binary to the boot partition at byte offset `0x40000` in flash memory using `dd if=u-boot.img of=/dev/mmcblk0boot0 bs=1k seek=256`.\n3. Create an ext4 root filesystem on user data partition 1 using `mkfs.ext4 /dev/mmcblk0p1`.\n4. Configure eMMC boot bus flags by issuing `mmc bootpart enable 1 1 /dev/mmcblk0` to enable ROM boot execution without error upon hardware reset and power cycle, ensuring persistent access to kernel storage partitions and secondary environment blocks."
