    "raw_asr": "migrating large android multi module billed two grad le version catalog provide centralized dependenci declarat and type safe accessor across subprojects in production environment create grad le slash libs dot versions dot toml in repository root and define version number under versions library artifact under librari and plugin identifier under plugins two declare project dependenci declaratively reference declared dependenci within subproject build dot grad le dot kts file using generated type safe catalog accessor like implementat libs dot androidx dot core dot ktx or implementat libs dot bundles dot retrofit this structure eliminates duplicated version string definit across billed file streamlines automated dependabot version bump and guarantees consistent library version across complex multi module android repository cleanly and reliably",
    "refined_text": "Migrating large Android multi-module builds to Gradle Version Catalogs provides centralized dependency declarations and type-safe accessors across subprojects in production environments. Create `gradle/libs.versions.toml` in your repository root and define version numbers under `[versions]`, library artifacts under `[libraries]`, and plugin identifiers under `[plugins]` to declare project dependencies declaratively.\n\nReference declared dependencies within subproject `build.gradle.kts` files using generated type-safe catalog accessors like `implementation(libs.androidx.core.ktx)` or `implementation(libs.bundles.retrofit)`. This structure eliminates duplicated version string definitions across build files, streamlines automated dependabot version bumps, and guarantees consistent library versions across complex multi-module Android repositories cleanly and reliably."
