    "refined_text": "Optimizing rendering performance in complex SwiftUI applications requires avoiding unnecessary body re-evaluations during state mutations. Decompose large monolithic view hierarchies into small granular SwiftUI `View` structs, ensuring each individual child view depends only on the specific sub-state parameters it renders onto the screen.\n\nAvoid initializing heavy computational objects or network controllers inside view initializers since SwiftUI recreates struct declarations repeatedly. Instead, instantiate long-lived objects inside state holders annotated with `@StateObject` or `.task`, and pass immutable values down the hierarchy to leverage SwiftUI internal equatable diffing for buttery smooth sixty frames-per-second scrolling."
