    "raw_asr": "in dual cloak asynchronous fifo design we convert read and write pointers from binary to gray code before passing them through double flip flop synchronizers to prevent multi bit transitions from sampling invalid pointer states during cloak domain crossing between read and write domains",
    "refined_text": "Convert write and read pointers from binary to gray code before transmitting them across clock domain boundaries in an asynchronous FIFO. Passing gray-coded pointers through two-stage flip-flop synchronizers ensures that only one bit changes per clock cycle.\n\nThis eliminates multi-bit sampling hazards and guarantees reliable full and empty flag generation across asynchronous clock boundaries."
