    "raw_asr": "evaluate finite state machine encoding styles in v h d l buy testing one hot versus binary encoding one hot encoding utilizes more flip flops but reduces l u t logic depth while binary encoding minimizes register count at expense of decode latency",
    "refined_text": "Analyze finite state machine encoding tradeoffs in VHDL by comparing one-hot and binary configurations. One-hot encoding assigns a dedicated flip-flop to each state, minimizing combinational next-state decoding logic and maximizing operating speed.\n\nIn contrast, binary encoding minimizes total register consumption but increases look-up table levels, making it suitable for resource-constrained architectures."
  },
