    "raw_asr": "to eliminate critical path setup timing violations across the sixty four bit arithmetic datapath running at one hundred fifty megahertz follow these optimization steps first inspect worst negative slack reports buy executing report timing dash max paths ten dash nworst one to pinpoint combinational carry chains second insert two pipeline register stages between the partial product multiplier and accumulator logic to split wide addition trees and break long combinational propagation third rebuild the design using vi va do synthesis directive explore and retiming to balance register distribution across d s p slices and verify zero negative slack",
    "refined_text": "Resolve critical setup timing violations across the 64-bit arithmetic datapath running at 150 MHz through structured pipeline optimization:\n1. Inspect worst negative slack paths by executing `report_timing -max_paths 10 -nworst 1` to isolate critical combinational carry chains and high-fanout nets.\n2. Insert two pipeline register stages between the partial product multiplier and accumulator logic to split wide addition trees and break long routing delays.\n3. Rebuild the design in Vivado using synthesis directive `-directive Explore` and enable `-retiming` to balance register distribution across DSP slices before re-running post-route timing analysis to confirm positive slack margins."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "to implement high throughput a x i four master controller capable of sustained burst transfers without protocol deadlocks follow this design architecture first decouple write address and write data channels buy registering aw valid and w valid through independent state machines without waiting four cross channel handshakes second track in flight burst requests using outstanding transacti counters and terminate data bursts cleanly buy driving w last on the final transfer beat third monitor b valid and b ready handshakes to capture b resp status codes before retiring write descriptors from the active queue ensuring buffer space frees up deterministically across backpressure cycles without stalling datapath stages",
    "refined_text": "Implement a high-throughput AXI4 master controller capable of sustained burst transfers without protocol deadlocks:\n1. Decouple address and data channels by registering `awvalid` and `wvalid` through independent finite state machines without waiting for cross-channel handshakes.\n2. Track in-flight burst requests using an outstanding transaction counter, and terminate data bursts cleanly by asserting `wlast` on the final transfer beat.\n3. Monitor `bvalid` and `bready` handshakes to capture write completion status codes `bresp` before retiring active transaction descriptors, ensuring that buffer space frees up deterministically across all backpressure cycles without stalling pipeline stages."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "to establish reliable cloak domain crossing verification flow across asynchronous fifo interfaces follow these engineering steps first define all independent clock sources and asynchronous groups in the dot s d c timing constraint file using set clock groups dash asynchronous to prevent false static timing paths second run cue sim c d c analysis to detect unconstrained domain crossings combinational glitches on control signals and improper synchroniz structures third replace multi bit signal crossings with gray code encoded pointers and verify that two flip flop synchronizers satisfy mean time between failure constraints eliminating metastability hazards and data corruption during live hardware operation",
    "refined_text": "Establish a reliable clock domain crossing verification flow across asynchronous FIFO interfaces using structured static checks:\n1. Define all independent clock sources and asynchronous clock relationships in the SDC timing constraint file using `set_clock_groups -asynchronous` to prevent false timing violations.\n2. Run Questa CDC static analysis to detect unconstrained domain crossings, combinational glitches on control signals, and improper synchronizer topologies across clock domains.\n3. Replace multi-bit signal crossings with gray-coded pointers and verify that two-stage synchronizer flip-flops satisfy required MTBF reliability targets, eliminating potential metastability hazards and data corruption during live hardware operation."
  },
