    "raw_asr": "to construct multi rate d s p decimation pipeline on f p g a hardware using polyphase fir filter architecture follow these design steps first partition symmetric filter impulse response into four polyphase sub filter coefficient sets to decrease effective multiplier operating frequency across channels second map multiply accumulate operations into cascaded d s p forty eight slices with internal pipeline registers enabled to satisfy timing closure at two hundred fifty megahertz without introducing combinational propagation stalls third buffer intermediate decimation samples into dual port block ram primitives and manage downstream sampling cadence using synchronous clock enable strobes preserving spectral signal integrity and dynamic range while streaming continuous baseband data",
    "refined_text": "Construct a multi-rate DSP decimation pipeline on FPGA hardware using polyphase FIR filter architectures and hardware blocks:\n1. Partition the symmetric filter impulse response into four polyphase sub-filter coefficient sets to decrease the effective multiplier operating frequency across channels.\n2. Map multiply-accumulate operations into cascaded DSP48 slices with internal pipeline registers enabled to satisfy timing closure at 250 MHz without introducing combinational propagation stalls.\n3. Buffer intermediate decimation samples into dual-port block RAM primitives and manage downstream sampling cadence using synchronous clock enable strobes, preserving spectral signal integrity and dynamic range while streaming continuous baseband data."
