    "refined_text": "Implement a robust asynchronous dual-clock FIFO leveraging embedded block RAM primitives and reliable pointer synchronizers:\n1. Configure the embedded block RAM in simple dual-port mode with independent write and read clock ports and appropriate `WRITE_FIRST` operating attributes.\n2. Maintain binary write and read counters while converting them to gray code before passing them through two-stage flip-flop synchronizers across clock domains.\n3. Derive full and empty status flags by comparing synchronized gray-code pointers to prevent buffer overflow or underflow hazards, ensuring that data words transfer across clock domains reliably without packet truncation or corruption."
