    "raw_asr": "to optimize high density arithmetic logic and memory block utilization in intel quar tus prime follow these synthesis and fitting recommendations first enable automatic register retiming and d s p block balancing within project settings file using set global assignment dash name auto d s p replacement on second group related multiplier blocks using logic lock region assignments to minimize interconnect routing delay surrounding embedded m twenty k memory blocks third execute quar tus timing analyzer using quar tus sta to verify maximum operating frequency f max across slow and fast silicon process corners ensuring that all arithmetic pipelines satisfy target throughput and production timing sign off margins",
    "refined_text": "Optimize high-density arithmetic logic and memory block utilization in Intel Quartus Prime using advanced fitter settings:\n1. Enable automatic register retiming and DSP block balancing within the project settings file using `set_global_assignment -name AUTO_DSP_REPLACEMENT ON` in the QSF.\n2. Group related multiplier blocks using Logic Lock region assignments to minimize interconnect routing delay surrounding embedded M20K memory blocks and prevent unrouted nets.\n3. Execute Quartus Timing Analyzer using `quartus_sta` to verify maximum operating frequency `fmax` across slow and fast silicon process corners, ensuring that all arithmetic pipelines satisfy target throughput and production timing sign-off margins."
