    "raw_asr": "to resolve stubborn holed and setup timing violations after routing in vi va do through iterative physical optimization passes follow this procedure first evaluate post route timing slack using report timing summary dash delay type min max dash check timing verbose to classify critical paths and identify localized holed hotspots second execute phys opt design dash directive explore with hold fix to allow physical synthesis engine to insert routing buffers without degrading setup margins on adjacent paths third inspect post optimization slack and perform incremental routing using route design dash preserve to finalize timing closure while preserving valid routes achieving clean sign off with zero setup violations and positive holed margins across all operating corners",
    "refined_text": "Resolve stubborn hold and setup timing violations after routing in Vivado through iterative physical optimization passes:\n1. Evaluate post-route timing slack using `report_timing_summary -delay_type min_max -check_timing_verbose` to classify critical paths and identify localized hold hotspots.\n2. Execute `phys_opt_design -directive ExploreWithHoldFix` to allow the physical synthesis engine to insert routing buffers without degrading setup margins on adjacent data paths.\n3. Inspect post-optimization slack and perform incremental routing using `route_design -preserve` to finalize timing closure while preserving valid routes, achieving clean sign-off with zero setup violations and positive hold margins across all operating corners."
