    "raw_asr": "to generate complete s d c timing constrains four external r g m i i gigabit ethernet interface operating at one hundred twenty five megahertz follow these steps first create primary transmit clock and virtual receiver clock in s d c file using create clock and create generated clock commands with explicit duty cycles second specify set input delay constrains with dash max and dash min parameters on receive data lines to account four board trace skew and phy output jitter third apply set output delay constrains relative to transmit clock to ensure proper setup and holed margins at external receiver guaranteeing error free packet reception and robust signal integrity under variable thermal conditions",
    "refined_text": "Generate complete SDC timing constraints for an external RGMII Gigabit Ethernet interface operating at 125 MHz:\n1. Create the primary transmit clock and a virtual receiver clock in the SDC file using `create_clock` and `create_generated_clock` commands with explicit duty cycles.\n2. Specify `set_input_delay` constraints with `-max` and `-min` parameters on receive data lines to account for board trace skew and PHY output jitter.\n3. Apply `set_output_delay` constraints relative to the transmit clock to ensure proper setup and hold margins at the external receiver, guaranteeing error-free packet reception and robust signal integrity under variable thermal conditions."
