    "refined_text": "Construct a comprehensive UVM verification environment for a round-robin packet arbiter using structured verification components:\n1. Create a `uvm_sequence_item` class defining packet length, traffic priority classes, and randomized payload byte streams to exercise protocol edge cases and corner traffic scenarios.\n2. Implement multi-channel UVM driver and reactive monitor components connected through SystemVerilog virtual interfaces to RTL arbiter request and grant pins.\n3. Design a scoreboard that tracks request arrival order, verifies fair round-robin scheduling across channels, and flags unexpected packet drops, ensuring that starvation never occurs under continuous randomized stimulus conditions."
