    "refined_text": "Ensure seamless cross-vendor synthesis of hierarchical VHDL-2008 designs across Vivado and Quartus using portable coding conventions:\n1. Declare all external entity ports using standard `std_logic` and `std_logic_vector` types rather than proprietary vendor library primitives or custom packages.\n2. Encapsulate shared constants and functions within VHDL-2008 packages, leveraging unconstrained array definitions and package generics to facilitate parameterization across multiple top-level project configurations.\n3. Avoid vendor-specific buffer primitives in behavioral logic by isolating clock trees and I/O buffers into dedicated top-level structural wrappers, maintaining clean separation between technology-independent logic and FPGA fabric primitives across diverse toolchains."
