    "refined_text": "Bring up a high-bandwidth DDR4 memory controller subsystem on FPGA hardware using vendor memory IP cores:\n1. Configure the memory interface IP core in Vivado targeting target DDR4 SDRAM components with matched timing parameters, memory geometries, and board trace delays.\n2. Connect the controller AXI4 slave port to the system interconnect, configuring base address mappings, burst length capabilities, and arbitration priorities.\n3. Verify memory calibration status by monitoring the `c0_init_calib_complete` signal and running read-write pattern tests across all address ranks, confirming write leveling, read centering, and zero bit error rates during continuous stress traffic."
