    "refined_text": "Minimize dynamic power consumption across high-density FPGA fabrics using structured architectural low-power techniques:\n1. Insert dedicated `BUFGCE` primitives to gate clock trees driving inactive datapath sections whenever enable signals remain deasserted, stopping switching activity at the root.\n2. Configure embedded block RAM primitives with dynamic power-down modes during extended read and write idle intervals to conserve static and dynamic power dissipation.\n3. Guide placement algorithms to cluster high-toggle nets into adjacent logic slices, reducing interconnect routing capacitance and overall switching dissipation without compromising timing closure on critical high-frequency arithmetic paths across varying thermal envelopes."
