    "refined_text": "Automate production board testing and FPGA programming on factory manufacturing lines using standardized boundary-scan procedures:\n1. Execute JTAG boundary-scan testing using vendor BSDL models to verify pin continuity and detect solder short circuits across high-density BGA balls and interconnect traces.\n2. Program external non-volatile SPI flash memory with golden production bitstreams using `openocd` or dedicated hardware programmer tools over automated scripts.\n3. Execute automated power-on self-test firmware over UART to validate onboard DDR memory, optical transceivers, and peripheral communications before flashing final production keys and issuing factory calibration certificates prior to unit packaging and customer deployment."
