    "refined_text": "Implementing a real-time edge multi-target tracking architecture combines periodic deep learning object detection with frame-to-frame optical flow motion tracking across streaming camera video.\n1. Execute YOLOv8 object detection every five video frames using `model.predict(frame, conf=0.5)` to discover new target bounding boxes and update track identities.\n2. Extract salient corner features within each active bounding box using `cv2.goodFeaturesToTrack` during intermediate video frames.\n3. Track extracted feature points forward in time using pyramidal Lucas-Kanade optical flow via `cv2.calcOpticalFlowPyrLK` to estimate bounding box displacements.\n4. Update target state vectors in a Kalman filter to smooth trajectory estimates and maintain persistent object tracks during temporary detector occlusions."
