    "refined_text": "Calibrating an industrial edge camera to map perspective video coordinates onto a planar ground coordinate system requires rigorous geometric transformation and accurate intrinsic parameter calculation across high-resolution calibration patterns.\n1. Detect chessboard corners across twenty calibration images using `cv2.findChessboardCorners` and refine subpixel coordinates with `cv2.cornerSubPix`.\n2. Compute the intrinsic camera matrix and lens distortion coefficients using `cv2.calibrateCamera` to undistort incoming camera frames before inference.\n3. Identify four ground-plane fiducial points and compute the planar homography matrix using `cv2.findHomography(src_pts, dst_pts, cv2.RANSAC, 3.0)`.\n4. Transform incoming camera frames into a top-down bird-eye view orthographic perspective using `cv2.warpPerspective` to calculate precise ground metric distance measurements for analytics."
