    "refined_text": "Conducting a standardized edge benchmarking harness on Jetson platforms requires measuring latency percentiles, throughput, and hardware power consumption simultaneously across sustained neural network evaluation runs.\n1. Lock hardware processor clocks to maximum operating frequencies using `sudo jetson_clocks` to eliminate thermal throttling variance during benchmarking.\n2. Launch a background hardware monitoring daemon logging GPU power draw and thermals using `tegrastats --logfile tegra.log --interval 100`.\n3. Benchmark the compiled TensorRT engine with `trtexec --loadEngine=detector.engine --warmUp=2000 --iterations=10000` to measure steady-state inference performance.\n4. Compute median, p95, and p99 latency percentiles while verifying zero memory leak degradation over continuous edge execution across twenty-four-hour test cycles."
