    "refined_text": "Postprocessing raw tensor predictions from a custom anchor-free YOLOv9 model involves decoding bounding box coordinates and eliminating redundant detections across dense spatial prediction grids.\n1. Slice the raw output tensor into bounding box regression offsets and class probability logits along the channel feature dimension.\n2. Apply the sigmoid activation function to class logits to compute confidence probabilities, and filter candidate predictions below a 0.4 threshold.\n3. Convert bounding box offsets from center-distance format into standard corner coordinates `[x1, y1, x2, y2]` scaled to image dimensions.\n4. Execute multiclass batched Non-Maximum Suppression with `torchvision.ops.batched_nms(boxes, scores, class_idxs, iou_threshold=0.5)` to yield final detection tensors for downstream tracking modules."
