    "refined_text": "Designing a fault-tolerant edge video ingestion service for remote RTSP cameras requires handling network dropouts and corrupted H.264 packets across lossy IP communication links.\n1. Configure a GStreamer capture pipeline using `rtspsrc location=rtsp://camera protocols=tcp latency=400` to ensure packet order integrity.\n2. Route the network stream into hardware accelerated `nvv4l2decoder ! nvvidconv ! video/x-raw, format=BGRx ! videoconvert ! appsink` for zero-overhead decoding.\n3. Implement a background watchdog thread in Python checking whether new frames arrive within a two-second timeout window.\n4. When network failure occurs, trigger clean pipeline teardown and initiate an exponential backoff reconnection loop until the video stream recovers and normal ingestion resumes."
