    "refined_text": "Ensuring thermal stability and preventing hardware clock throttling on Jetson Orin under continuous vision workloads requires precise power budgeting and proactive thermal management controls.\n1. Set the system power envelope to 15W operating mode using `sudo nvpmodel -m 1` to cap peak power consumption.\n2. Lock CPU, GPU, and memory controller clocks to predetermined deterministic frequencies using `sudo jetson_clocks`.\n3. Configure dynamic fan control policy in `/etc/nvfancontrol.conf` with aggressive thermal trip points starting at sixty-five degrees Celsius.\n4. Continuously monitor temperature metrics and power rail draw using `tegrastats` to verify that junction temperatures remain safely below critical throttling thresholds during high computational load."
