    "raw_asr": "execute this short time fourier transform extraction pipeline in python to generate high resolution spectral representations four machine learning speech recognition models one load the raw multichannel waveform at forty eight kilohertz mono float format using s f dot read audio underscore path comma dtype equals quote float thirty two quote from the soundfile library two partition the continuous time domain signal into overlapping frames with a window length of two zero four eight samples and a hop size of five one two samples three apply a periodic hann window function across each extracted audio frame to suppress side lobe spectral leakage before computing the discrete fourier transform four compute the complex s t f t matrix using torch dot stft signal comma n underscore f f t equals two zero four eight comma hop underscore length equals five one two comma return underscore complex equals true and convert magnitude bins into logarithmic decibel scale values",
    "refined_text": "Execute this Short-Time Fourier Transform extraction pipeline in Python to generate high-resolution spectral representations for machine learning speech recognition models.\n1. Load the raw multichannel waveform at 48kHz mono float format using `sf.read(audio_path, dtype='float32')` from the `soundfile` library.\n2. Partition the continuous time-domain signal into overlapping frames with a window length of 2048 samples and a hop size of 512 samples.\n3. Apply a periodic Hann window function across each extracted audio frame to suppress side-lobe spectral leakage before computing the discrete Fourier transform.\n4. Compute the complex STFT matrix using `torch.stft(signal, n_fft=2048, hop_length=512, return_complex=True)` and convert magnitude bins into logarithmic decibel scale values."
