    "raw_asr": "follow this procedural configuration guide to optimize the pipe wire daemon and wire plumber session manager four real time professional audio workstations and low latency production environments one create the system drop in configuration directory and file at slash etc slash pipewire slash pipewire dot conf dot d slash ninety nine dash proaudio dot conf to override default buffer settings two define the fixed processing clock buy specifying default dot clock dot rate equals forty eight thousand and default dot clock dot quantum equals one two eight within the main configuration context block three configure wire plumber al sa device profiles in slash etc slash wireplumber slash main dot lua dot d slash fifty dash alsa dash config dot lua to enforce fixed period sizes and disable auto suspend power saving modes four restart the user audio services with system see tee ell dash dash user restart pipewire pipewire dash pulse wireplumber and verify clock lock using p w dash metadata dash n settings",
    "refined_text": "Follow this procedural configuration guide to optimize the PipeWire daemon and WirePlumber session manager for real-time professional audio workstations and low-latency production environments.\n1. Create the system drop-in configuration directory and file at `/etc/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/99-proaudio.conf` to override default buffer settings.\n2. Define the fixed processing clock by specifying `default.clock.rate = 48000` and `default.clock.quantum = 128` within the main configuration context block.\n3. Configure WirePlumber ALSA device profiles in `/etc/wireplumber/main.lua.d/50-alsa-config.lua` to enforce fixed period sizes and disable auto-suspend power saving modes.\n4. Restart the user audio services with `systemctl --user restart pipewire pipewire-pulse wireplumber` and verify clock lock using `pw-metadata -n settings`."
