    "raw_asr": "implement this frequency domain partition convolution pipeline using the overlap save method to execute zero latency impulse response reverbs one pad the impulse response of length m with trailing zeros to reach f f t frame size n equals l plus m minus one where n is an exact power of two two compute and cache the forward discrete fourier transform of the zero padded impulse response using f f t w underscore plan underscore d f t underscore r two c underscore one d open paren close paren three buffer incoming streaming input blocks of l samples concatenate the trailing m minus one samples from the previous block and compute the forward f f t four multiply the complex spectral vectors point wise execute the inverse f f t and discard the initial m minus one circular convolution artifacts to recover clean output",
    "refined_text": "Implement this frequency-domain partition convolution pipeline using the overlap-save method to execute zero-latency impulse response reverbs.\n1. Pad the impulse response of length `M` with trailing zeros to reach FFT frame size `N = L + M - 1` where `N` is an exact power of two.\n2. Compute and cache the forward discrete Fourier transform of the zero-padded impulse response using `fftw_plan_dft_r2c_1d()`.\n3. Buffer incoming streaming input blocks of `L` samples, concatenate the trailing `M - 1` samples from the previous block, and compute the forward FFT.\n4. Multiply the complex spectral vectors point-wise, execute the inverse FFT, and discard the initial `M - 1` circular convolution artifacts to recover clean output."
