    "refined_text": "Follow this mastering export workflow using SoX to downsample high-resolution studio audio while preserving low-level dynamic detail across musical releases.\n1. Inspect the source file sample rate and bit depth using `soxi master_96k24b.wav` to verify input audio headroom.\n2. Resample the master from 96kHz to standard distribution 44.1kHz using the very high quality linear-phase SoX resampler via `rate -v -L 44100`.\n3. Apply a brickwall peak normalization stage using `norm -0.5` to prevent inter-sample clipping during consumer digital reconstruction.\n4. Reduce bit depth from 24-bit to 16-bit PCM by applying triangular probability density function dithering with noise shaping using `dither -s -p 16`."
