    "refined_text": "Follow this setup guide to establish a kernel-level ALSA loopback soundcard and stream synchronized low-latency audio over local networks to broadcast clients.\n1. Load the ALSA virtual loopback kernel module by running `modprobe snd-aloop index=1 id=Loopback pcm_substreams=8` with administrative privileges.\n2. Verify module initialization and locate the newly assigned virtual capture and playback devices by querying `cat /proc/asound/cards`.\n3. Route primary application audio output directly into virtual subdevice `hw:Loopback,0,0` using custom ALSA client environment variables.\n4. Stream the captured audio from `hw:Loopback,1,0` across the network to remote listening clients via `ffmpeg -f alsa -i hw:Loopback,1,0 -c:a libopus -b:a 192k -f rtp rtp://192.168.1.50:5004`."
  },
