    "raw_asr": "follow this digital signal processing procedure to design a complementary fourth order linkwitz riley acoustic crossover filter network in python four multi way loudspeaker systems one define the acoustic crossover split frequency at twenty five hundred hertz with an operating hardware sample rate of forty eight thousand hertz two design two cascaded second order butterworth low pass filters using sci py dot signal dot butter two comma twenty five hundred comma b type equals quote low quote comma f s equals forty eight thousand comma output equals quote s o s quote to form a twenty four d b per octave low pass branch three generate the identical matched high pass branch using sci py dot signal dot butter two comma twenty five hundred comma b type equals quote high quote comma f s equals forty eight thousand comma output equals quote s o s quote to guarantee phase alignment four sum the complex frequency response curves across the crossover region to confirm zero magnitude ripple and flat butterworth response at the transition frequency",
    "refined_text": "Follow this digital signal processing procedure to design a complementary fourth-order Linkwitz-Riley acoustic crossover filter network in Python for multi-way loudspeaker systems.\n1. Define the acoustic crossover split frequency at 2500Hz with an operating hardware sample rate of 48000Hz.\n2. Design two cascaded second-order Butterworth low-pass filters using `scipy.signal.butter(2, 2500, btype='low', fs=48000, output='sos')` to form a 24dB-per-octave low-pass branch.\n3. Generate the identical matched high-pass branch using `scipy.signal.butter(2, 2500, btype='high', fs=48000, output='sos')` to guarantee phase alignment.\n4. Sum the complex frequency response curves across the crossover region to confirm zero magnitude ripple and flat Butterworth response at the transition frequency."
