    "refined_text": "Follow this measurement procedure using JACK latency diagnostic utilities to calculate precise hardware round-trip audio latency through physical analog to digital converters.\n1. Connect a physical loopback audio patch cable directly from soundcard analog line output 1 into line input 1.\n2. Start the JACK audio server with the target buffer period configuration via `jackd -d alsa -d hw:0 -r 48000 -p 64 -n 2`.\n3. Launch the round-trip latency analyzer utility in your terminal window by running `jack_iodelay`.\n4. Connect diagnostic signal ports using `jack_connect jack_delay:out system:playback_1` and `jack_connect system:capture_1 jack_delay:in` to measure internal driver and converter delay in sample frames."
