    "raw_asr": "execute this compound f f m peg audio filtering command chain to clean voice recordings remove low frequency plosives and tame harsh vocal sibilance across studio podcast tracks and broadcast voice recordings one apply an eighty hertz high pass filter using highpass equals f equals eighty to eliminate low frequency microphone handling noise mechanical rumble and room vibrations two attenuat nasal boxiness buy notching out four hundred hertz using a parametric peaking equalizer filter via equalizer equals f equals four hundred colon width underscore type equals q colon w equals two point zero colon g equals minus four point five three suppress vocal sibilance between five kilohertz and eight kilohertz using a specialized dynamic de esser stage configured with deesser equals i equals zero point five colon m equals zero point five colon f equals zero point five four smooth dynamic performance fluctuations and prevent inter sample clipping buy chaining compand equals attacks equals zero point zero three colon decays equals zero point three colon points equals minus eighty slash minus eighty pipe minus twenty slash minus twenty pipe zero slash minus six into a true peak limiter with ceiling set to minus one d b t p",
    "refined_text": "Execute this compound FFmpeg audio filtering command chain to clean voice recordings, remove low-frequency plosives, and tame harsh vocal sibilance across studio podcast tracks and broadcast voice recordings.\n1. Apply an 80Hz high-pass filter using `highpass=f=80` to eliminate low-frequency microphone handling noise, mechanical rumble, and room vibrations.\n2. Attenuate nasal boxiness by notching out 400Hz using a parametric peaking equalizer filter via `equalizer=f=400:width_type=q:w=2.0:g=-4.5`.\n3. Suppress vocal sibilance between 5kHz and 8kHz using a specialized dynamic de-esser stage configured with `deesser=i=0.5:m=0.5:f=0.5`.\n4. Smooth dynamic performance fluctuations and prevent inter-sample clipping by chaining `compand=attacks=0.03:decays=0.3:points=-80/-80|-20/-20|0/-6` into a true-peak limiter with ceiling set to `-1.0dBTP`."
