    "refined_text": "Follow this configuration procedure to establish bit-perfect ALSA audio routing and bypass software resampling distortions on audiophile DACs.\n1. Identify the hardware card index, device number, and supported native bit formats by examining `/proc/asound/card0/pcm0p/sub0/hw_params`.\n2. Open `/etc/asound.conf` and define a direct hardware type device block `pcm.audiophile { type hw card 0 device 0 }` to circumvent dmix attenuation.\n3. Disable software volume scaling by binding the control interface directly with `ctl.audiophile { type hw card 0 }`.\n4. Test uncompressed bit-perfect playback of a 24-bit 96kHz stream using `aplay -D audiophile -f S24_3LE -r 96000 -c 2 test_track.wav` and verify stream hardware parameters."
