    "refined_text": "Follow this administrative procedure to establish synchronized RTP audio multicasting across local network zones using PulseAudio sound server daemon modules in production streaming environments.\n1. Load the RTP sender sink module into the master audio server by executing `pactl load-module module-null-sink sink_name=rtp_sink`.\n2. Bind the null sink monitor to a multicast RTP transport using `pactl load-module module-rtp-send source=rtp_sink.monitor destination_ip=224.0.0.56 port=46400`.\n3. On receiving client listener machines, launch the RTP reception listener by running `pactl load-module module-rtp-recv sap_address=224.0.0.56`.\n4. Route active media playback streams into `rtp_sink` via `pactl move-sink-input` to broadcast synchronized multi-room audio with deterministic packet buffering across connected local networks."
