    "refined_text": "Implement this lock-free Single Producer Single Consumer ring buffer in C++ to transfer audio data safely between real-time and worker threads.\n1. Allocate a contiguous backing buffer memory array with capacity constrained strictly to an exact power of two.\n2. Define atomic integer head and tail indices using `std::atomic<size_t>` with `std::memory_order_relaxed` and `std::memory_order_acquire` constraints.\n3. Write incoming audio samples from the producer thread into the buffer using fast bitwise modulo indexing `index & (capacity - 1)` before storing the updated head with `std::memory_order_release`.\n4. Read samples from the consumer audio callback thread without taking mutex locks to prevent priority inversion and preserve real-time execution deadlines."
