    "refined_text": "Create and deploy an enterprise IBM Spectrum Scale shared filesystem across distributed storage nodes with network shared disks for high-performance scientific workloads and parallel analytics.\n\n1. Define the network shared disk descriptor file and create storage targets by executing `mmcrnsd -F /root/nsd_descriptor.txt -v yes` across storage servers.\n2. Generate the distributed cluster filesystem using `mmcrfs gpfs2 -F /root/nsd_descriptor.txt -A yes -B 4M -m 2 -M 3 -r 2 -R 3` with 4MB block size.\n3. Mount the new distributed file system across all compute cluster nodes by running `mmmount gpfs2 -a` and inspect disk state with `mmlsdisk gpfs2` to ensure high availability and continuous data replication."
