    "refined_text": "Implement and calibrate the Slurm multifactor priority plugin to enforce balanced fairshare utilization and job ordering across diverse research groups in the supercomputer cluster environment.\n\n1. Configure priority calculation parameters in `/etc/slurm/slurm.conf` by setting `PriorityType=priority/multifactor` and assigning `PriorityDecayHalfLife=14-0` for rolling historical decay across departments and user accounts.\n2. Assign relative evaluation weights by setting `PriorityWeightFairshare=1000000`, `PriorityWeightAge=100000`, and `PriorityWeightPartition=50000` alongside `PriorityWeightJobSize=20000` across scheduling queues and establish initial job priority baselines.\n3. Reload cluster configuration using `scontrol reconfigure` and examine effective user priority factors by inspecting the detailed diagnostic output of `sshare -a -l` to guarantee equitable resource distribution and prevent job queue starvation."
