    "refined_text": "Profile memory subsystem performance and eliminate non-uniform memory access latency penalties on multi-socket supercomputer compute nodes running bandwidth-bound numerical workloads.\n\n1. Generate the hardware topology visualization and cache hierarchy tree by executing `lstopo --output-format console` and inspecting socket CPU core masks with `numactl --show`.\n2. Compile the STREAM benchmark with aggressive vectorization compiler flags and bind execution threads to local NUMA nodes using `numactl --cpunodebind=0 --membind=0 ./stream_c.exe`.\n3. Measure Triad memory bandwidth across all sockets by exporting `OMP_NUM_THREADS=64` and comparing benchmark results against interleaved memory allocation via `numactl --interleave=all` to assess memory bus scaling and bandwidth limits on compute nodes."
