    "raw_asr": "remediate degraded lus tre object storage targets and evacuate critical simulation data before uncorrectable drive failures occur inside the production parallel storage array infrastructure one identify degraded or failing o s t components buy inspecting system logs and querying storage target health using l c t l get param osc dot state across all mounted client systems two mark the degraded target as read only to halt incoming write traffic buy running l c t l conf param scratch o s t zero zero zero eight dot osc dot active equals zero on the central m g s node three migrate existing datasets off the failing target buy invoking l f s find slash scratch dash o scratch o s t zero zero zero eight pipe l f s migrate dash y dash s to preserve research data integrity and rebalance cluster storage capacity without downtime",
    "refined_text": "Remediate degraded Lustre object storage targets and evacuate critical simulation data before uncorrectable drive failures occur inside the production parallel storage array infrastructure.\n\n1. Identify degraded or failing OST components by inspecting system logs and querying storage target health using `lctl get_param osc.*.state` across all mounted client systems.\n2. Mark the degraded target as read-only to halt incoming write traffic by running `lctl conf_param scratch-OST0008.osc.active=0` on the central MGS node.\n3. Migrate existing datasets off the failing target by invoking `lfs find /scratch -O scratch-OST0008 | lfs_migrate -y -s` to preserve research data integrity and rebalance cluster storage capacity without downtime."
