    "refined_text": "Configure Slurm burst buffer plugins to automate dataset staging between parallel filesystems and high-speed local NVMe storage pools for high-throughput input pipelines on supercomputers.\n\n1. Define burst buffer parameters in `/etc/slurm/burst_buffer.conf` specifying `StageInTimeout=1800` and `ValidateAccessResource=true` for local NVMe storage pools to manage parallel file transfers.\n2. Include staging directives in user batch submission scripts using `#BB stage_in source=/lustre/data/input.bin destination=/nvme/scratch/input.bin type=file` before executing high-speed I/O operations.\n3. Submit the burst buffer workflow using `sbatch job.slurm` and monitor staging lifecycle transitions with `scontrol show bbstat` until compute resources initialize and execution begins successfully without storage bottlenecks prior to launching numerical calculation kernels."
