    "refined_text": "Investigate and mitigate distributed CUDA memory exhaustion and associated NCCL collective synchronization timeouts during large-scale transformer training on supercomputer clusters across multiple racks.\n\n1. Inspect job log traces to distinguish between fatal CUDA out-of-memory errors on rank zero and downstream `NCCL watchdog timeout` failures on secondary worker nodes across the cluster.\n2. Enable PyTorch CUDA memory caching optimization by exporting `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True` and increasing `NCCL_ASYNC_ERROR_HANDLING=1` inside the job execution script.\n3. Re-launch the training run with reduced per-device batch sizes and enable gradient checkpointing inside the batch submission script via `sbatch train_distributed.slurm` to ensure stable convergence across all ranks without unexpected crashes."
