    "refined_text": "Configure hierarchical Quality of Service tiers and job preemption policies to enable immediate execution of high-priority emergency workloads across production supercomputer partitions and queues.\n\n1. Define QoS levels in the Slurm database using `sacctmgr add qos emergency Priority=10000 PreemptMode=requeue,cancel` and create normal tier with `Priority=100` for regular cluster submissions.\n2. Associate authorized user accounts with the emergency QoS tier by executing `sacctmgr modify user name=hpcadmin set qos=emergency,normal` across the scheduling database.\n3. Submit the urgent simulation script using `sbatch --qos=emergency job.slurm` and verify that low-priority batch jobs are preempted and requeued cleanly without corrupting active job state across nodes under the updated preemption rules."
