    "refined_text": "Configure and validate OpenMP target offloading to NVIDIA GPUs for high-order Fortran numerical simulation codes executing across accelerated cluster architectures in production environments.\n\n1. Compile the computational routines using `nvfortran -mp=gpu -gpu=cc80,cuda11.8 -Minfo=mp ./simulation.f90 -o sim.exe` targeting Ampere architecture with optimized GPU kernel compilation.\n2. Verify OpenMP target region mapping and kernel execution by exporting `LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=-1` and `NVCOMPILER_ACC_NOTIFY=3` before job launch to trace asynchronous GPU host transfers and ensure accurate device memory allocation.\n3. Execute the offloaded benchmark under Slurm allocation using `srun --nodes=1 --gres=gpu:1 ./sim.exe` and profile memory transfers with `nsys profile ./sim.exe` to confirm kernel speedup and register usage."
