    "refined_text": "To implement a custom SQLite Virtual File System that provides encrypted storage and crash-resilient atomic sector writes, execute this complete development sequence across application storage layers.\n\n1. Subclass the `sqlite3_vfs` structure, assigning function pointers for standard OS system operations including `xOpen`, `xRead`, `xWrite`, `xSync`, and `xFileControl`.\n2. Implement an atomic write strategy within `xWrite` and `xSync` that enforces 4096-byte sector alignment and calls `fdatasync()` to prevent torn page writes on unexpected power loss events.\n3. Register the new virtual file system globally using `sqlite3_vfs_register()` with `make_default = 1` before invoking `sqlite3_open_v2()` in application connection threads to mount the custom engine."
