    "raw_asr": "like to implement a concurrent high performance mem table for l s m trees that supports lock free reader threads during high speed writes follow this development workflow in c plus plus first construct an arena memory allocator that allocates large contiguous memory slabs avoiding malloc overhead and eliminating thread synchronization during node space allocation in resident ram second implement a multi level concurrent skiplist using atomic forward pointers to support lock free search queries while concurrent writer threads append records to memory third insert new keys using compare and swap c a s primitives to link forward pointers at each tower height updating the total memory byte counter atomically without mutex locking",
    "refined_text": "To implement a concurrent high-performance MemTable for LSM trees that supports lock-free reader threads during high-speed writes, follow this development workflow in C++ systems.\n\n1. Construct an arena memory allocator that allocates large contiguous memory slabs, avoiding malloc overhead and eliminating thread synchronization during node space allocation in resident RAM.\n2. Implement a multi-level concurrent SkipList using atomic `std::atomic<Node*>` forward pointers to support lock-free search queries while concurrent writer threads append records to memory.\n3. Insert new keys using compare-and-swap CAS primitives to link forward pointers at each tower height, updating the total memory byte counter atomically without mutex locking."
