    "refined_text": "To configure RocksDB for multi-terabyte datasets without exceeding physical RAM capacity in production storage servers, execute this two-level partitioned index procedure on instances across the distributed cluster fleet.\n\n1. Set `BlockBasedTableOptions::index_type = BlockBasedTableOptions::IndexType::kTwoLevelIndexSearch` to enable hierarchical index partitioning within SSTable data files on disk.\n2. Configure `partition_filters = true` and `metadata_block_size = 4096` to subdivide massive Bloom filter blocks into discrete 4KB partitions matching physical disk block boundaries.\n3. Enable `cache_index_and_filter_blocks_with_high_priority = true` and allocate a dedicated LRU block cache to keep top-level index partitions permanently resident in memory while lower level partitions page dynamically into the block cache during query operations."
