  {
    "raw_asr": "inspecting individual quality control reports across hundreds of sequencing samples wastes significant manual analysis time aggregate individual fast q c and sam tools flag stat metrics across all sample directories buy running multi q c slash data slash project dash o slash data slash qc report to generate a consolidated interactive h t m l dashboard tracking metrics",
    "refined_text": "Inspecting individual quality control reports across hundreds of sequencing samples wastes significant manual analysis time.\n\nAggregate individual FastQC and `samtools flagstat` metrics across all sample directories by running `multiqc /data/project/ -o /data/qc_report/` to generate a consolidated interactive HTML dashboard tracking alignment percentages, duplication rates, and base quality distributions across batches."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "execute a complete germline variant discovery pipeline on raw illumina paired end reads across standard production environments first trim low quality bases and illumina adapters buy running fast p dash i read one dot f q dash i read two dot f q dash o clean one dot f q dash o clean two dot f q dash dash detect adapter four pe to generate high quality reads second align the trimmed reads two human reference genome h g thirty eight and sort buy coordinate using b w a mem two mem dash t sixteen h g thirty eight dot f a clean one dot f q clean two dot f q pipe sam tools sort dash at four dash o aligned dot sorted dot b a m to create indexed alignments third caul germline single nucleotide variants and short indels using g a t k haplotype caller dash r h g thirty eight dot f a dash i aligned dot sorted dot b a m dash o germline variants dot v c f to produce clinical grade variant calls across targeted chromosomes",
    "refined_text": "Execute a complete germline variant discovery pipeline on raw Illumina paired-end sequencing reads across standard production environments to generate high-confidence genotype calls.\n\n1. Trim low-quality bases and Illumina adapters by running `fastp -i read1.fq -I read2.fq -o clean1.fq -O clean2.fq --detect_adapter_for_pe` to generate clean paired reads.\n2. Align the trimmed reads to human reference genome `hg38.fa` and sort by coordinate using `bwa-mem2 mem -t 16 hg38.fa clean1.fq clean2.fq | samtools sort -@ 4 -o aligned.sorted.bam`.\n3. Call germline single-nucleotide variants and short indels using `gatk HaplotypeCaller -R hg38.fa -I aligned.sorted.bam -O germline_variants.vcf` to produce clinical-grade variant calls for downstream genomic interpretation."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "perform an end to end r n a seq differential expression workflow from raw sequencing data across multiple experimental biological replicates to identify differentially expressed transcripts first align paired end reads two the reference genome while generating coordinate sorted alignments buy executing star dash dash genome dir star index dash dash read f i l e s in r one dot f q r two dot f q dash dash out sam type b a m sorted by coordinate dash dash out file name prefix sample one to obtain sorted alignments second assign aligned fragments two annotated gene exons buy running feature counts dash p dash s two dash a gencode dot g t f dash o gene counts dot t x t sample one aligned dot sorted by coord dot out dot b a m to produce gene level raw count matrices third conduct differential expression analysis and shrinkage estimation in r buy executing d e seq data set from matrix followed buy d e seq and l f c shrink to calculate log fold changes and adjusted p values across all tested experimental conditions",
    "refined_text": "Perform an end-to-end RNA-seq differential expression workflow from raw sequencing data across multiple experimental biological replicates to identify significantly perturbed genes.\n\n1. Align paired-end reads to the reference genome while generating coordinate-sorted alignments by executing `STAR --genomeDir star_index/ --readFilesIn r1.fq r2.fq --outSAMtype BAM SortedByCoordinate --outFileNamePrefix sample1_`.\n2. Assign aligned fragments to annotated gene exons by running `featureCounts -p -s 2 -a gencode.gtf -o gene_counts.txt sample1_Aligned.sortedByCoord.out.bam` to produce gene-level raw count matrices.\n3. Conduct differential expression analysis and empirical Bayes shrinkage estimation in R by executing `DESeqDataSetFromMatrix` followed by `DESeq()` and `lfcShrink()` to calculate log2 fold changes, Wald test statistics, and false discovery rates across conditions."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "isolate high confidence somatic single nucleotide mutations from matched tumor and normal paired tissues through systematic filtering and annotation across clinical cancer specimens first execute somatic variant calling using g a t k mutect two dash r h g thirty eight dot f a dash i tumor dot b a m dash i normal dot b a m dash normal normal sample dash o somatic raw dot v c f to generate candidate mutations second filter candidate variants against cross sample contamination and orientation bias buy running g a t k filter mutect calls dash r h g thirty eight dot f a dash v somatic raw dot v c f dash o somatic filtered dot v c f to isolate real mutations third annotate functional impacts on ensembl transcript models buy running snip eff dash v h g thirty eight somatic filtered dot v c f greater than somatic annotated dot v c f to prioritize actionable oncogenic driver mutations for therapeutic evaluation and biomarker discovery across cohorts",
    "refined_text": "Isolate high-confidence somatic single-nucleotide mutations from matched tumor and normal paired tissues through systematic filtering and annotation across clinical cancer specimens.\n\n1. Execute somatic variant calling using `gatk Mutect2 -R hg38.fa -I tumor.bam -I normal.bam -normal normal_sample -O somatic_raw.vcf` to generate candidate somatic mutations.\n2. Filter candidate variants against cross-sample contamination, germline penetrance, and sequencing orientation bias by running `gatk FilterMutectCalls -R hg38.fa -V somatic_raw.vcf -O somatic_filtered.vcf`.\n3. Annotate functional impacts on Ensembl transcript models by running `snpEff -v hg38 somatic_filtered.vcf > somatic_annotated.vcf` to prioritize actionable oncogenic driver mutations, frameshifts, and missense alterations for therapeutic evaluation and targeted clinical biomarker discovery across patient cohorts."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "polish a denovo pac bio hi fi microbial genome assembly and identify consensus errors across assembled contig boundaries to achieve complete contiguous chromosomes first align high accuracy hi fi reads two the draft contigs buy running mini map two dash a x map dash hifi dash dash secondary equals no draft dot f a hifi dot f a s t q pipe sam tools sort dash at eight dash o hifi aligned dot b a m to create coordinate sorted alignments second index the coordinate sorted b a m file and evaluate read coverage uniformity buy running sam tools index hifi aligned dot b a m and sam tools depth dash a hifi aligned dot b a m to verify depth third caul consensus variants and fix remaining assembly base errors buy running free bayes dash f draft dot f a dash p one hifi aligned dot b a m greater than polish cauls dot v c f to generate polished consensus sequences for downstream circularization",
    "refined_text": "Polish a de novo PacBio HiFi microbial genome assembly and identify consensus errors across assembled contig boundaries to achieve complete contiguous chromosomes.\n\n1. Align high-accuracy HiFi reads to draft contigs by running `minimap2 -ax map-hifi --secondary=no draft.fa hifi.fastq | samtools sort -@ 8 -o hifi_aligned.bam` to generate coordinate-sorted alignments.\n2. Index the coordinate-sorted BAM file and evaluate read coverage uniformity by running `samtools index hifi_aligned.bam` and `samtools depth -a hifi_aligned.bam` to verify depth across repetitive intervals.\n3. Call consensus variants and fix remaining assembly base errors by running `freebayes -f draft.fa -p 1 hifi_aligned.bam > polish_calls.vcf` to produce accurate polished consensus sequences for downstream circularization and plasmid annotation."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "process targeted deep amplicon sequencing libraries containing unique molecular identifiers four ultra sensitive variant detection at low variant allele frequencies across liquid biopsy samples first extract u m i sequences from raw f a s t q headers and append them two read tags buy running u m i dash tools extract dash dash bc pattern equals n n n n n n n n dash dash stdin equals read one dot f q dash dash read two in equals read two dot f q second map u m i tagged reads two the human reference and sort buy coordinate using b w a mem two mem dash t eight h g thirty eight dot f a reads dot extracted dot f q pipe sam tools sort dash o aligned dot b a m third group reads buy genomic coordinates and u m i barcodes buy calling u m i dash tools group dash i aligned dot b a m dash dash output bam equals grouped dot b a m to consolidate identical molecules and calculate consensus depths",
    "refined_text": "Process targeted deep amplicon sequencing libraries containing unique molecular identifiers for ultra-sensitive variant detection at low variant allele frequencies across liquid biopsy samples.\n\n1. Extract UMI sequences from raw FASTQ headers and append them to read tags by running `umi_tools extract --bc-pattern=NNNNNNNN --stdin=read1.fq --read2-in=read2.fq`.\n2. Map UMI-tagged reads to the human reference and sort by coordinate using `bwa-mem2 mem -t 8 hg38.fa reads.extracted.fq | samtools sort -o aligned.bam`.\n3. Group reads by genomic coordinates and UMI barcodes by calling `umi_tools group -i aligned.bam --output-bam=grouped.bam` to consolidate identical PCR duplicates, resolve sequencing errors, and calculate deduplicated consensus depths across targeted loci."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "quantify single cell r n a sequencing droplets and generate cell buy gene count matrices using salmon alevin four downstream cell clustering and marker gene discovery across heterogeneous tissue samples first build a decoy aware transcriptome index buy executing salmon index dash t transcripts dot f a dash d decoys dot t x t dash i salmon index dash k thirty one to map reads accurately second perform droplet cellular barcode demultiplexing u m i deduplication and transcript quantification buy running salmon alevin dash l i s r dash one read one dot f q dash two read two dot f q dash dash chromium dash i salmon index dash o alevin out dash dash tg map txp two gene dot t s v third import the binary count matrix into seurat or scanpy buy parsing the generated quants mat dot g z and quants mat rows dot t x t files four cluster validation and differential expression",
    "refined_text": "Quantify single-cell RNA sequencing droplets and generate cell-by-gene count matrices using salmon alevin for downstream cell clustering and marker gene discovery across heterogeneous tissue samples.\n\n1. Build a decoy-aware transcriptome index by executing `salmon index -t transcripts.fa -d decoys.txt -i salmon_index -k 31` to map reads accurately.\n2. Perform droplet cellular barcode demultiplexing, UMI deduplication, and transcript quantification by running `salmon alevin -l ISR -1 read1.fq -2 read2.fq --chromium -i salmon_index -o alevin_out --tgMap txp2gene.tsv`.\n3. Import the binary count matrix into Seurat or Scanpy by parsing the generated `quants_mat.gz` and `quants_mat_rows.txt` files for unsupervised cell-type annotation, quality filtering, and cell cluster validation."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "recalibrate base quality scores on whole exome sequencing alignments two remove systematic machine errors prior two germline variant calling and indel realignment workflows first build the empirical recalibration model against known polymorphic sites buy running g a t k base recalibrator dash r h g thirty eight dot f a dash i raw aligned dot b a m dash dash known sites d b s n p dot v c f dash o recal data dot table second apply the recalibrated base scores two the input alignment buy executing g a t k apply b q s r dash r h g thirty eight dot f a dash i raw aligned dot b a m dash dash b q s r recal file recal data dot table dash o recalibrated dot b a m third calculate mapping statistics and confirm recalibration quality buy executing sam tools flag stat recalibrated dot b a m to verify alignment depth duplication rate and proper mate pairs across targets",
    "refined_text": "Recalibrate base quality scores on whole exome sequencing alignments to remove systematic machine errors prior to germline variant calling and indel realignment workflows.\n\n1. Build the empirical recalibration model against known polymorphic sites by running `gatk BaseRecalibrator -R hg38.fa -I raw_aligned.bam --known-sites dbsnp.vcf -O recal_data.table`.\n2. Apply the recalibrated base scores to the input alignment by executing `gatk ApplyBQSR -R hg38.fa -I raw_aligned.bam --bqsr-recal-file recal_data.table -O recalibrated.bam`.\n3. Calculate comprehensive mapping statistics and confirm recalibration quality by executing `samtools flagstat recalibrated.bam` to verify target alignment depth, duplication rate, mean insert size, and proper mate pairs across all targeted capture intervals."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "characterize large genomic structural variants from oxford nanopore long read sequencing data across complex repetitive regions and segmental duplications in human genomes first align long reads two the reference genome while generating comprehensive c i g a r strings using mini map two dash a x map dash ont dash dash md ref dot f a ont reads dot f q pipe sam tools sort dash at eight dash o ont sorted dot b a m second index the coordinate sorted long read b a m file buy running sam tools index ont sorted dot b a m to prepare alignments third identify deletions insertions inversions and translocations buy running cute s v ont sorted dot b a m ref dot f a sv output dot v c f work dir dash dash max split count ten dash dash min support ten to filter artifactual split reads and output validated structural variants",
    "refined_text": "Characterize large genomic structural variants from Oxford Nanopore long-read sequencing data across complex repetitive regions and segmental duplications in human genomes.\n\n1. Align long reads to the reference genome while generating comprehensive CIGAR strings using `minimap2 -ax map-ont --MD ref.fa ont_reads.fq | samtools sort -@ 8 -o ont_sorted.bam`.\n2. Index the coordinate-sorted long-read BAM file by running `samtools index ont_sorted.bam` to prepare alignments for regional querying and visual inspection in genome browsers.\n3. Identify deletions, insertions, inversions, and translocations by running `cuteSV ont_sorted.bam ref.fa sv_output.vcf work_dir/ --max_split_count 10 --min_support 10` to output validated structural variants with precise breakpoint resolution across all human chromosomes."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "profile taxonomic composition in shotgun metagenomic sequencing reads while filtering host background from clinical biological specimens and complex environmental samples first subtract human host contaminating reads buy aligning f a s t q files against the human genome using bow tie two dash x h g thirty eight dash one r one dot f q dash two r two dot f q dash dash un conc host free dot f q pipe sam tools view dash b dash o host aligned dot b a m second assign taxonomic classifications two microbial reads buy executing kraken two dash dash db standard dash dash paired host free dot one dot f q host free dot two dot f q dash dash report kraken report dot t x t third estimate species level relative abundances buy running bracken dash d standard dash i kraken report dot t x t dash o bracken abundance dot t x t to reestimate species distributions from k mer classifications",
    "refined_text": "Profile taxonomic composition in shotgun metagenomic sequencing reads while filtering host background from clinical biological specimens and complex environmental samples.\n\n1. Subtract human host contaminating reads by aligning FASTQ files against the human genome using `bowtie2 -x hg38 -1 r1.fq -2 r2.fq --un-conc host_free.fq | samtools view -b -o host_aligned.bam`.\n2. Assign taxonomic classifications to microbial reads by executing `kraken2 --db standard --paired host_free.1.fq host_free.2.fq --report kraken_report.txt`.\n3. Estimate species-level relative abundances by running `bracken -d standard -i kraken_report.txt -o bracken_abundance.txt` to reestimate species distributions from k-mer classifications and compute empirical abundance estimates for each detected bacterial and viral clade."
  },
