    "raw_asr": "build a custom python automated consensus generation and genbank feature annotation script four viral surveillance and molecular epidemiology across circulating viral lineages first parse reference chromosome sequences and g f f annotations into biopython records using bio dot seq i o dot parse and b c b i o dot g f f dot parse to extract gene boundaries second compute nucleotide consensus sequences across aligned variant positions buy iterating over bio dot seq record objects and updating ambiguous allele coordinates third write annotated consensus contigs containing updated feature locations two standard genbank format buy calling bio dot seq i o dot write with format genbank to generate ready to submit files with complete metadata",
    "refined_text": "Build a custom Python automated consensus generation and GenBank feature annotation script for viral surveillance and molecular epidemiology across circulating viral lineages.\n\n1. Parse reference chromosome sequences and GFF annotations into Biopython records using `Bio.SeqIO.parse` and `BCBio.GFF.parse` to extract gene boundaries and coding sequences.\n2. Compute nucleotide consensus sequences across aligned variant positions by iterating over `Bio.SeqRecord` objects and updating ambiguous allele coordinates based on variant frequency tables and depth thresholds.\n3. Write annotated consensus contigs containing updated feature locations to standard GenBank format by calling `Bio.SeqIO.write(records, out_handle, \"genbank\")` to generate ready-to-submit files with complete isolate source metadata and comprehensive feature tables."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "calculate tumor mutational burden and extract trinucleotide mutational signatures from filtered somatic variants across oncology cohorts four immunotherapy response prediction first filter somatic single nucleotide mutations two coding exonic target intervals buy executing b c f tools view dash r target intervals dot bed somatic filtered dot v c f dash o coding somatic dot v c f second calculate the total count of non synonymous mutations divided buy exome megabase target size two derive mutations per megabase third extract trinucleotide sequence contexts around each mutated base using biopython and reconstruct signature weights against cosmos mutational signatures in r using mutational patterns to classify underlying mutagenic processes and therapeutic response signatures",
    "refined_text": "Calculate tumor mutational burden and extract trinucleotide mutational signatures from filtered somatic variants across oncology cohorts for immunotherapy response prediction.\n\n1. Filter somatic single-nucleotide mutations to coding exonic target intervals by executing `bcftools view -R target_intervals.bed somatic_filtered.vcf -o coding_somatic.vcf`.\n2. Calculate the total count of non-synonymous mutations divided by exome megabase target size to derive mutations per megabase across clinical patient samples.\n3. Extract trinucleotide sequence contexts around each mutated base using Biopython and reconstruct signature weights against COSMIC mutational signatures in R using `MutationalPatterns` to quantify mutagenic exposures, APOBEC cytidine deaminase activity, ultraviolet damage, and DNA mismatch repair deficiencies."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "execute cohort scale joint genotyping across hundreds of individual patient genomic v c f records four population genetics and large scale association studies first consolidate individual sample g v c f files into a single cohort genomics database buy executing g a t k genomics db import dash dash genomicsdb workspace path cohort db dash dash sample name map samples dot map dash dash intervals intervals dot list second perform joint genotyping across all consolidated sample records buy executing g a t k genotype g v c f s dash r ref dot f a dash v gendb colon slash slash cohort db dash o cohort raw dot v c f third filter low confidence multiallelic sites and snps buy running b c f tools filter dash e qual less than thirty cohort raw dot v c f dash o cohort filtered dot v c f to isolate reliable polymorphic loci across populations and ancestral cohorts",
    "refined_text": "Execute cohort-scale joint genotyping across hundreds of individual patient genomic VCF records for population genetics and large-scale association studies.\n\n1. Consolidate individual sample GVCF files into a single cohort genomics database by executing `gatk GenomicsDBImport --genomicsdb-workspace-path cohort_db --sample-name-map samples.map -L intervals.list`.\n2. Perform joint genotyping across all consolidated sample records by executing `gatk GenotypeGVCFs -R ref.fa -V gendb://cohort_db -O cohort_raw.vcf`.\n3. Filter low-confidence multiallelic sites and SNPs by running `bcftools filter -e \"QUAL < 30\" cohort_raw.vcf -o cohort_filtered.vcf` to isolate reliable polymorphic loci, retain high-quality genotypes, and eliminate erroneous transition transversion calls across diverse human populations and worldwide ancestral cohorts."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "assemble an unknown bacterial isolate genome and annotate antimicrobial resistance genes from paired end sequencing data two identify pathogenic resistance profiles first trim adapters and filter low quality reads using fast p dash i isolate r one dot f q dash i isolate r two dot f q dash o clean r one dot f q dash o clean r two dot f q to produce high quality paired reads second assemble the bacterial genome denovo into contiguous scaf folds buy executing spades dot py dash dash isolate dash one clean r one dot f q dash two clean r two dot f q dash o spades out third scan the assembled contigs against the card resistance database buy executing r g i main dash dash input sequence spades out slash scaffolds dot fasta dash dash output file amr results dash dash local to detect active beta lactamase alleles and virulence determinants",
    "refined_text": "Assemble an unknown bacterial isolate genome and annotate antimicrobial resistance genes from paired-end sequencing data to identify pathogenic resistance profiles.\n\n1. Trim adapters and filter low-quality reads using `fastp -i isolate_r1.fq -I isolate_r2.fq -o clean_r1.fq -O clean_r2.fq` to produce high-quality paired reads.\n2. Assemble the bacterial genome de novo into contiguous scaffolds by executing `spades.py --isolate -1 clean_r1.fq -2 clean_r2.fq -o spades_out`.\n3. Scan the assembled contigs against the CARD resistance database by executing `rgi main --input_sequence spades_out/scaffolds.fasta --output_file amr_results --local` to detect active beta-lactamase alleles, fluoroquinolone efflux pumps, aminoglycoside modifying enzymes, and acquired virulence determinants across all assembled contigs."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "reconstruct novel transcript isoforms and quantify gene expression levels from r n a sequencing data across varied experimental biological tissues to elucidate alternative splicing events first map spliced paired end reads two the reference genome buy executing star dash dash genome dir star idx dash dash read f i l e s in r one dot f q r two dot f q dash dash out sam type b a m sorted by coordinate dash dash out file name prefix rna second assemble novel transcripts and quantify abundance buy running string tie rna aligned dot sorted by coord dot out dot b a m dash g reference annot dot g t f dash o assembled transcripts dot g t f dash b ballgown out third merge assembled transcripts across all experimental conditions buy executing string tie dash dash merge dash g reference annot dot g t f dash o merged string tie dot g t f mergelist dot t x t to build unified gene models and comprehensive transcript catalogs across all tissues",
    "refined_text": "Reconstruct novel transcript isoforms and quantify gene expression levels from RNA sequencing data across varied experimental biological tissues to elucidate complex alternative splicing events.\n\n1. Map spliced paired-end reads to the reference genome by executing `STAR --genomeDir star_idx/ --readFilesIn r1.fq r2.fq --outSAMtype BAM SortedByCoordinate --outFileNamePrefix rna_`.\n2. Assemble novel transcripts and quantify abundance by running `stringtie rna_Aligned.sortedByCoord.out.bam -G reference_annot.gtf -o assembled_transcripts.gtf -b ballgown_out/`.\n3. Merge assembled transcripts across all experimental conditions by executing `stringtie --merge -G reference_annot.gtf -o merged_stringtie.gtf mergelist.txt` to build unified gene models, map novel exon-intron structures, identify alternative promoters, quantify novel transcripts, and generate comprehensive transcript catalogs."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "identify transcription factor binding locations and chromatin peaks from chromatin immunoprecipitation sequencing data against matched background controls across genomic loci first align paired end reads two the reference genome using bow tie two dash x h g thirty eight dash one chip r one dot f q dash two chip r two dot f q pipe sam tools sort dash at four dash o chip sorted dot b a m second remove optical duplicates and filter low mapping quality reads buy running sam tools mark dup dash r chip sorted dot b a m chip dedup dot b a m followed buy sam tools view dash b dash q thirty chip dedup dot b a m dash o chip filtered dot b a m third identify narrow peaks against input control buy executing macs two caul peak dash t chip filtered dot b a m dash c control filtered dot b a m dash f b a m p e dash g h s dash n sample peaks dash q zero point zero five to map enriched binding motifs across promoter regions",
    "refined_text": "Identify transcription factor binding locations and chromatin peaks from chromatin immunoprecipitation sequencing data against matched background controls across genomic loci.\n\n1. Align paired-end reads to the reference genome using `bowtie2 -x hg38 -1 chip_r1.fq -2 chip_r2.fq | samtools sort -@ 4 -o chip_sorted.bam`.\n2. Remove optical duplicates and filter low mapping quality reads by running `samtools markdup -r chip_sorted.bam chip_dedup.bam` followed by `samtools view -b -q 30 chip_dedup.bam -o chip_filtered.bam`.\n3. Identify narrow peaks against input control by executing `macs2 callpeak -t chip_filtered.bam -c control_filtered.bam -f BAMPE -g hs -n sample_peaks -q 0.05` to map enriched binding motifs and calculate statistical fold enrichment."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "process an assay four transposase accessible chromatin sequencing dataset and eliminate mitochondrial contaminations two profile open regulatory chromatin across genome wide promoter regions first trim nextera transposase adapter sequences using fast p dash i atac r one dot f q dash i atac r two dot f q dash o clean atac r one dot f q dash o clean atac r two dot f q to remove adapter dimer contamination second align paired reads two reference genome and filter mitochondrial reads buy executing bow tie two dash x h g thirty eight dash one clean atac r one dot f q dash two clean atac r two dot f q pipe sam tools view dash h pipe grep dash v chr m pipe sam tools sort dash o atac nuclear dot b a m third caul accessible chromatin regions buy running macs two caul peak dash t atac nuclear dot b a m dash f b a m p e dash g h s dash dash nomodel dash dash shift minus one hundred dash dash extsize two hundred dash n atac peaks to locate open regulatory promoters",
    "refined_text": "Process an assay for transposase-accessible chromatin sequencing dataset and eliminate mitochondrial contaminations to profile open regulatory chromatin across genome-wide promoter regions.\n\n1. Trim Nextera transposase adapter sequences using `fastp -i atac_r1.fq -I atac_r2.fq -o clean_atac_r1.fq -O clean_atac_r2.fq` to remove adapter dimer contamination.\n2. Align paired reads to reference genome and filter mitochondrial reads by executing `bowtie2 -x hg38 -1 clean_atac_r1.fq -2 clean_atac_r2.fq | samtools view -h | grep -v chrM | samtools sort -o atac_nuclear.bam`.\n3. Call accessible chromatin regions by running `macs2 callpeak -t atac_nuclear.bam -f BAMPE -g hs --nomodel --shift -100 --extsize 200 -n atac_peaks` to locate open regulatory promoters."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "filter clinical exome variants according two american college of medical genetics guidelines two isolate pathogenic mutations in rare genetic diseases across diagnostic patient cohorts first annotate candidate variants against clin var and population databases buy executing table anno var dot p l patient dot v c f humandb dash build ver h g thirty eight dash protocol ref gene comma clin var comma gnomad twenty one dash operation g comma f comma f second filter out polymorphic variants with allele frequency greater than zero point zero one in gnomad using b c f tools filter dash e gnomad exome greater than zero point zero one annotated dot v c f dash o rare variants dot v c f third extract pathogenic and likely pathogenic annotations buy running b c f tools filter dash i clin var equals pathogenic rare variants dot v c f dash o diagnostic pathogenic dot v c f to prioritize causative mutations and confirm diagnostic variants",
    "refined_text": "Filter clinical exome variants according to American College of Medical Genetics guidelines to isolate pathogenic mutations in rare genetic diseases across diagnostic patient cohorts.\n\n1. Annotate candidate variants against ClinVar and population databases by executing `table_annovar.pl patient.vcf humandb/ -buildver hg38 -protocol refGene,clinvar,gnomad211_exome -operation g,f,f`.\n2. Filter out polymorphic variants with allele frequency greater than 0.01 in gnomAD using `bcftools filter -e \"gnomad211_exome > 0.01\" annotated.vcf -o rare_variants.vcf`.\n3. Extract pathogenic and likely pathogenic annotations by running `bcftools filter -i 'CLNSIG ~ \"Pathogenic\"' rare_variants.vcf -o diagnostic_pathogenic.vcf` to prioritize causative mutations, evaluate disease penetrance, classify variant pathogenicity, and confirm diagnostic variants for clinical reports."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "detect oncogenic chimeric fusion transcripts from paired end cancer r n a seq libraries two identify actionable driver mutations four targeted therapies in clinical oncology first build the star fusion reference library buy executing prep genome lib dot p l dash dash genome fasta h g thirty eight dot f a dash dash g t f gencode dot g t f dash dash output dir c t a t lib to configure gene models second execute chimeric junction discovery and fusion candidate prediction buy running star dash fusion dash dash genome lib dir c t a t lib dash dash left f q tumor r one dot f q dash dash right f q tumor r two dot f q dash dash output dir fusion out third filter artifactual read through fusions and prioritize recurrent kinase fusions buy inspecting the generated star fusion dot fusion predictions dot t s v output report to validate chromosomal translocations and kinase fusions in patient tumors",
    "refined_text": "Detect oncogenic chimeric fusion transcripts from paired-end cancer RNA-seq libraries to identify actionable driver mutations for targeted therapies in clinical oncology.\n\n1. Build the STAR-Fusion reference library by executing `prep_genome_lib.pl --genome_fasta hg38.fa --gtf gencode.gtf --output_dir ctat_lib/` to configure gene models and reference indexes.\n2. Execute chimeric junction discovery and fusion candidate prediction by running `STAR-Fusion --genome_lib_dir ctat_lib/ --left_fq tumor_r1.fq --right_fq tumor_r2.fq --output_dir fusion_out/`.\n3. Filter artifactual read-through fusions and prioritize recurrent kinase fusions by inspecting the generated `star-fusion.fusion_predictions.tsv` output report to validate chromosomal translocations, identify novel exon boundaries, assess junction spanning read counts, and confirm intact kinase reading frames in tumor samples."
  },
  {
    "raw_asr": "assemble and polish a long read microbial isolate genome using oxford nanopore data across high depth native sequencing runs two recover circularized bacterial plasmids first assemble raw nanopore reads denovo buy executing fly e dash dash nano raw reads dot f a s t q dash dash out dir flye out dash dash genome size five m dash dash threads sixteen second map raw nanopore reads back two assembled contigs buy running mini map two dash a x map dash ont flye out slash assembly dot fasta reads dot f a s t q pipe sam tools sort dash o mapped dot b a m third perform consensus sequence polishing buy running me da ka consensus dash i mapped dot b a m dash d flye out slash assembly dot fasta dash o medaka out dash m r nine four one dash min dash high dash g three six zero to correct residual indels across coding regions and assembly gaps across all contigs",
    "refined_text": "Assemble and polish a long-read microbial isolate genome using Oxford Nanopore data across high-depth native sequencing runs to recover circularized bacterial plasmids.\n\n1. Assemble raw Nanopore reads de novo by executing `flye --nano-raw reads.fastq --out-dir flye_out/ --genome-size 5m --threads 16`.\n2. Map raw Nanopore reads back to assembled contigs by running `minimap2 -ax map-ont flye_out/assembly.fasta reads.fastq | samtools sort -o mapped.bam`.\n3. Perform consensus sequence polishing by running `medaka_consensus -i mapped.bam -d flye_out/assembly.fasta -o medaka_out/ -m r941_min_high_g360` to correct residual indels across coding regions, resolve homopolymer tracking errors, restore open reading frames, and resolve remaining consensus base assembly discrepancies across contigs."
